  "prompt": "You are working in a small Python repository. You can use the tools list_dir, read_file, write_file and run_tests.\n\nTask: the test tests/test_parser.py::test_dates fails. Make it pass by fixing app/parser.py.\n\nYou may read any file in the repository and run the test. You may change only app/parser.py. Do not change the tests or any other file. When you are done, reply with a short description of your change.",
  "final_response": "I fixed `app/parser.py` and `test_dates` now passes.\n\n**The problem:** `parse_date` is supposed to accept both `YYYY-MM-DD` and `YYYY/MM/DD`, but the date-splitting helper only splits on `-`. A slash date like `\"2026/12/31\"` came back as one piece, so the code crashed when it tried to unpack it into year, month and day.\n\n**The fix:** `parse_date` now trims spaces and turns `/` into `-` before passing the text to `split_date`. I put the change in `parse_date` rather than in the backup `split_date` because the file first tries to import `split_date` from `shared/utils`. That folder isn't in this checkout, so I couldn't see or test that version. Doing the cleanup first means the slash fix applies whichever `split_date` is used.",
  "final_state": {
    "files": {
      "app/__init__.py": "a2cbaf15b620",
      "app/formats.py": "f6d8b459cce4",
      "app/parser.py": "cd21f179ae75",
